<%- include('../partials/top') %>

<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/careers">Careers</a></li><li>Interview questions</li></ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Interview question bank</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Useful from both sides of the table. If you are interviewing candidates, these are
      questions that produce evidence rather than rehearsed answers.
    </p>
    <div class="inset inset--brand">
      <p class="mb-0">
        <strong>Preparing?</strong> Do not memorise answers. Prepare five stories &mdash; a
        recovery, a failure, a difficult stakeholder, a team you improved, and a decision you got
        wrong &mdash; each with numbers in it. Almost every question below can be answered from
        one of those five.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% bank.forEach(function (t) { %>
    <section class="mb-6">
      <h2><%= t.theme %></h2>
      <div class="panel panel--brand">
        <p class="mb-0"><strong>What they are listening for.</strong> <%= t.forCandidates %></p>
      </div>
      <ul class="list-spaced mt-4">
        <% t.questions.forEach(function (qq) { %><li><%= qq %></li><% }) %>
      </ul>
    </section>
  <% }) %>

  <div class="panel">
    <h2 class="mt-0">If you are the one interviewing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask for specifics until you reach a number, a date or a name. Vague answers are usually
        vague experience.</li>
      <li>Follow up every success story with "what would you do differently?". The answer
        separates people who reflect from people who narrate.</li>
      <li>Use the same questions for every candidate, score against agreed criteria written
        before you started, and score independently before you discuss. It is the single most
        effective debiasing measure available and it costs nothing.</li>
      <li>Tell candidates the format in advance, including who they will meet and what each stage
        assesses. Withholding it does not test resilience, it tests luck.</li>
      <li>Give feedback to unsuccessful candidates. The delivery community is small and you will
        meet them again.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-0">
      Released under <a href="/legal/licence">CC BY 4.0</a> &mdash; put it in your hiring pack.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/bottom') %>
